From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:55:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: feed the SDHC the 19.2 MHz TCXO

sdhci-msm programs the DLL's FLL frequency field (DLL_CONFIG_2[17:10]) as
card clock * 4 / rate of the "xo" clock, and expects that clock to be the
19.2 MHz TCXO, as on SM8550 and SM8650 and as the vendor kernel hardcodes.
On SM8750 the SDHC was given RPMH_CXO_CLK, which runs at 38.4 MHz, so the
field was programmed at half its value: 22 instead of 43 for SDR104.
The 16 tuning phases then spanned two bit periods instead of one.

Feed the SDHC the 19.2 MHz bi_tcxo_div2 like the other blocks here do.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
index 6f2114c..5c25c2a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -3045,7 +3045,7 @@
 
 			clocks = <&gcc GCC_SDCC2_AHB_CLK>,
 				 <&gcc GCC_SDCC2_APPS_CLK>,
-				 <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK>;
+				 <&bi_tcxo_div2>;
 			clock-names = "iface",
 				      "core",
 				      "xo";
